Q: PHP equivalent of SQL&#39;s %like% A: <p>In addition to the solutions above, if you are trying to do like with multiple parts like "%absc%ehf%", following script will help. You need to put different parts as different elements in array. Here, array would be array('absc','ehf') </p>

<pre><code>// mainStr is the string you are searching and $partsArray holds the like parts 
// in array like explained above 
function like($mainStr, $partsArray) {
  if (empty($partsArray)) {
      return true;
  }

  $lastIndex = 0;
  // checks to see that strings exist after each other. In the example above, 
  // "%absc%ehf%" would first check the existence of absc and then if it exists 
  // it would continue checking the rest of the string for the rest of like parts 
  foreach($partsArray as $part) {
     $pos = strpos($mainStr, $part);
    if ( $pos === false || $pos &lt; $lastIndex) {
        return false;
    } 
    $lastIndex += $pos + strlen($part); 
  }
  return true;

}
</code></pre>
